[Music]  there has been a very hot debate in the  past year over transgender rights and  some backlash in the area of women's  sports swimmer leah thomas made  headlines this month when she became the  first openly transgender person to win a  division one national title now some  women criticize her participation saying  that she had an unfair advantage growing  up as a biological male the issue is  playing out in state legislatures 11  states now have laws restricting  transgender girls from playing female  sports and this week the republican  governors of utah and indiana vetoed  similar new restrictions utah  legislators are expected to override  that veto a new three-part series  highlights what it's like to be  transgender in america right now it's  called trans youth town hall executive  producer and host raquel willis  interviews people of all ages about  their experiences in this clip the  panelists describe what trans joy means  to them  my trans joy is my art when people know  us as who we are and not what we are  trans joy for me is all about the love  and care that flows between friends  family community and me definitely doing  things i love with the people i love and  everything is just happy flowers coming  out of my heart the series will air on  logo a division of paramount raquel  willis joins us right now how you doing  good morning good morning so glad to be  here thank you for joining us now the  town hall creates this safe space for  conversations about the transgender  community  how does it feel to be part of something  like this  it feels beautiful i mean i think one of  the most amazing parts of the series is  that just kind of cut through all of the  fodder all of the rhetoric that's out  there and talk directly to trans youth  we're humanizing we're letting people  empathize with their stories  yeah i think you know this may sound  silly but i think many people need a  trans 101 class if you will raquel could  you just briefly explain exactly what it  means and tell us a little bit about  your own personal story absolutely i  mean being trans is really not  identifying with the gender i was  assigned at birth so for instance i was  assigned male at birth i am a woman and  it's been a journey for me i think we  all have struggles around gender because  there are so many expectations that  we're all kind of forced to meet and for  many of us those boxes that were put in  don't fit for us when did you realize  for yourself you said you were born a  male when did you realize that this  isn't really who i am well how did you  struggle with that yeah well i was  assigned male at birth and i really had  a lot of struggles growing up because i  never quite fit in with all the  standards that were put out there for  for boys essentially and so my mom you  know is one of my biggest supporters and  she when i told her i was trans and i  was figuring out my gender identity once  i was in college she was like oh okay  this makes a lot of sense because i've  seen your journey through along the  years  now  we hear you mention the word struggle  quite a bit and some of those struggles  we hear about in the transgender  community it's violence and tragedy  but you decided in this town hall to  bring up the words trans joy because you  wanted to show some positivity within  the community um explain what trans joy  is yeah i mean trans joy is really kind  of the backbone of our community a lot  of people don't know trans people have  been around for centuries this is not a  new phenomenon  absolutely and so now we have more  language than ever before and we know  more about our history some of these  legendary figures like marsha p johnson  sylvia rivera and so many more for  education absolutely so it's about  education it's about us communing  together and understanding that there's  something beautiful about knowing your  truth and being able to fully stand in  it you know one of the things that i  thought was so great is the panel you  have is knockout and you all cover a lot  of different topics including sports and  including health what can you tell us  about that yeah well i think one of the  things that people will hear in the news  right now obviously all the talk about  the anti-trans legislation but what does  it really mean to be a young trans  person right now and what are the things  that trans people need to access i mean  these young people are just like every  other young person they need to be able  to have access to health care to  education and to their passions whether  it's sports the arts and beyond dale  mentioned earlier leah thomas the  swimmer who just won a division  one title i believe and there are people  on both sides saying support her she can  play any sport that she wants and then  there's other people saying well um my  daughter was a daughter it was a young  lady since birth and she fought her  whole life to compete and now she's  competing with somebody who might have  an unfair advantage what are your  thoughts on that well i think we have to  understand that what makes any athlete  elite  is different across the board so there  are a lot of these ideas around looking  at certain factors of trans people's  bodies trans people's hormone levels all  those different things  but we  have to be looking at people  holistically and i think one of the more  important things for us to think about  is what about access when i think about  young black trans athletes have they had  access to all of the training that maybe  their white counterparts have been able  to so a lot of times we're also thinking  about class as well right what you what  do you want people to take away real  quick from the town hall yeah well i  want people to understand that trans  people are just like every other person  you know we're all in our lives trying  to figure out the best path forward and  we all  deserve to live our best lives we are  all trying to figure it out that is that  we appreciate you appreciate you  bringing that joy to the show this  morning raquel willis thank you so much  you can watch her town hall series on  logo we'll be right back

